From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:26:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): fall back to the session's model and effort

A turn that pins nothing still ran on some model: the agent's configured
default, or whatever the harness last reported for the session. The agent
span now says so instead of leaving gen_ai.request.model and
gen_ai.response.model unset until a harness reports usage.

The runner already reads the session snapshot for the session span
attributes, so it adds, at no extra cost, omnigent.agent.model (the
agent's configured model), omnigent.session.model with
omnigent.session.model.source, and omnigent.session.reasoning_effort to
every span of the turn. The session model is the harness's last report
(observed), else the session's override (requested), else the configured
model (resolved_default); the source is inferred, since a snapshot
llm_model that differs from the configured model is a harness report.

On the agent span, gen_ai.request.model falls back to the configured
model, and gen_ai.response.model with omnigent.model.source is stamped
from the session model at turn start until an observed value replaces it
at turn end. Nothing changes when telemetry is off.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
